 "background": "Set at the springs of Lake Ohrid. Biljana is bleaching linen for her dowry when a caravan of wine merchants passes. She falls for the young man leading it, only to learn he is getting married that Sunday. Versions appear in folk-song collections from 1860 and 1861, and the motif of a girl and passing merchants runs from Ohrid to the Black Sea. Belograd is the old Slavic name for Berat in Albania. The last verse is a playful curse: may the river carry him to her, may a snake bite him with her teeth.",
